 ### Fast mode rate limits
 
-When using fast mode with `speed: "fast"` on Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Opus 5, or Claude Opus 4.8, dedicated rate limits apply that are separate from standard Opus rate limits. Claude Opus 5.5 has a default fast mode rate limit in the Start, Build, and Scale tiers, so you don't need to request access to use fast mode with it. Organizations in the Evaluation tier can use fast mode with Claude Opus 5.5 once they move to the Start, Build, or Scale tier. Fast mode for Claude Opus 5 and Claude Opus 4.8 is in research preview. To see your fast mode rate limits, go to the Rate limits page in the Claude Console. When fast mode rate limits are exceeded, the API returns a `429` error with a `retry-after` header.
+When you use fast mode with `speed: "fast"` on Claude Fable 5.2, Claude Mythos 5.2, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Opus 5, or Claude Opus 4.8, dedicated rate limits apply. They are separate from standard rate limits. Claude Opus 5.5 has a default fast mode rate limit in the Start, Build, and Scale tiers, so you don't need to request access to use fast mode with it. Organizations in the Evaluation tier can use fast mode with Claude Opus 5.5 once they move to the Start, Build, or Scale tier. The same applies to Claude Fable 5.2. It also applies to Claude Mythos 5.2. Fast mode for Claude Opus 5 and Claude Opus 4.8 is in research preview. To see your fast mode rate limits, go to the Rate limits page in the Claude Console. When you exceed your fast mode rate limits, the API returns a `429` error with a `retry-after` header.
 
 The response includes `anthropic-fast-*` headers that indicate your fast mode rate limit status. See Fast mode rate limits for details on these headers.
